- Never replace a React page with a serialized HTML blob, an AURA_DESIGN_MARKUP constant, or dangerouslySetInnerHTML.
- Never paste the full snapshot into a string constant or wrap the page in a raw HTML injector.
- Preserve existing component structure, imports, handlers, state, and routing unless a specific change requires updating them.
- If the edited snapshot changes content, structure, styling, images, icons, or links, reflect those changes in code.
- When Aura's asset picker changed image, background image, Spline, Unicorn, video, or background component sources, update those exact visual assets in the React project instead of treating the request as a no-op.
- Only change literal copy when the edited snapshot actually changes that copy. Never invent, append, or paraphrase text that is unchanged between the original and edited snapshots.
- Write normal JSX/TSX source code. Do not emit serialized source fragments, dangling quotes, half-open template literals, or literal escape sequences like \\n, \\t, or \\" into JSX unless they are intentionally part of runtime string content.
- The content field in each file edit must decode to raw file source only. Do not double-stringify the file source, and do not leave trailing JSON characters like "}, }, or ] inside the decoded code.
- Before returning, verify that every edited file has balanced JSX tags, parentheses, braces, quotes, and template literals.

