areable subdomains, connect custom domains, and manage CMS content without leaving the design flow."},{icon:Lue,title:"Advanced Design Mode",text:"Tune layers, breakpoints, spacing, components, snippets, responsive states, and visual details after generation without restarting the page."}],VGs=[{area:"Best use case",aura:"High-craft landing pages, SaaS sites, portfolios, templates, HTML exports, and design-to-code handoff.",lovable:"Full-stack app prototypes where backend, auth, and integrations matter more than visual polish.",figma:"Functional prototypes and interactive UI experiments inside a Figma-centered workflow.",v0:"React, Next.js, and Vercel-oriented apps with GitHub sync and deployment in the same ecosystem."},{area:"Usage model",aura:"Predictable prompt credits: 1 credit = 1 prompt across AI models.",lovable:"Usage-based credits deducted by message, with cost depending on message complexity.",figma:"Available for Full seats on paid Figma plans, with trial access on other seats and plans.",v0:"Credits are consumed from input and output token usage, including chat history and project context."},{area:"Starting quality",aura:"Pro templates, 1,400+ components, 20,000+ assets, snippets, and @ references give the model strong ingredients.",lovable:"Business and Enterprise workspaces can reuse design templates by copying full project codebases.",figma:"Can attach existing Figma designs, Community content, and design system packages to guide Make.",v0:"Strong React defaults, framework awareness, visual Design Mode, and Vercel deployment patterns."},{area:"Visual control",aura:"Advanced Design Mode with layers, measurements, auto breakpoints, component replacement, and visual editing.",lovable:"Visual edits and an in-app editor, with most work still shaped through the chat and generated project.",figma:"Designed for conversational iteration plus code editing, while staying close to Figma artifacts.",v0:"Design Mode for visual edits alongside generated React code and project files."},{area:"Output ownership",aura:"Standard HTML, Tailwind CSS, and vanilla JavaScript. Export full sites, host anywhere, or send to Figma.",lovable:"Exports generated app code and syncs with GitHub, often centered around app architecture and integrations.",figma:"Creates functional prototypes and web apps from Figma context, strongest inside the Figma ecosystem.",v0:"Generates React-oriented code with Vercel deployment, GitHub sync, and framework-specific context."},{area:"Where Aura wins",aura:"Fast craft, predictable iteration cost, reusable pro ingredients, CMS, exportability, and design-mode refinement.",lovable:"Choose it when full-stack backend generation is the main job and visual distinctiveness is secondary.",figma:"Choose it when the source of truth must remain in Figma and prototypes need designer review.",v0:"Choose it when your team is already committed to React, Next.js, and Vercel workflows."}],QGs=["1,700+ templates","1,400+ components","20,000+ assets","100 pages per Pro site","HTML and Figma export","Full CMS on Pro"],GGs=[{icon:Wu,title:"Pick the vibe",text:"Start from a pro template that already has hierarchy, spacing, type, and motion worth preserving."},{icon:jA,title:"Reference the ingredients",text:"Add @hero, @pricing, @testimonial, @animation-snippet, or a previous iteration to give the model exact context."},{icon:Xm,title:"Refine visually",text:"Use Design Mode for spacing, layers, responsive breakpoints, component swaps, colors, images, and CMS content."},{icon:PN,title:"Ship real HTML",text:"Publish, export the full site, continue in Cursor or v0, or send the result back into Figma."}],g1n=[{question:"Is Aura meant to replace Lovable, Figma Make, or v0?",answer:"Not always. Aura is strongest when the job is design quality, HTML output, templates, components, CMS, and visual refinement. Lovable is often better for full-stack MVPs, Figma Make for Figma-native prototypes, and v0 for React or Vercel-heavy builds."},{question:"What makes Aura different from token-metered tools?",answer:"Aura keeps generation usage simple: one prompt maps to one credit across AI models. That makes experimentation easier to budget than workflows where longer prompts, attachments, history, and large outputs can change the token cost."},{question:"Can I still use Aura output with other tools?",answer:"Yes. Aura exports standard HTML, Tailwind CSS, and vanilla JavaScript. You can host it, keep editing in a code editor, move pieces into v0 or Cursor, or export designs to Figma."},{question:"Why do templates and @ references matter?",answer:"AI design tools are only as good as their context. Aura lets you reference real templates, components, snippets, and previous iterations so the generated page follows proven structure instead of inventing every decision from scratch."}],JGs=[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage",name:"Aura vs Lovable vs Figma Make vs v0",description:"A practical comparison of Aura, Lovable, Figma Make, and v0 for AI web design, app generation, HTML export, templates, components, CMS, and visual editing.",url:"https://aura.build/aura-vs-lovable-vs-figma-make-vs-v0",dateModified:"2026-04-27",publisher:{"@type":"Organization",name:"Aura",url:"https://aura.build"}},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage",mainEntity:g1n.map(e=>({"@type":"Question",name:e.question,acceptedAnswer:{"@type":"Answer",text:e.answer}}))}],XGs=[{label:"Aura pricing",href:"https://www.aura.build/pricing"},{label:"Aura docs",href:"https://www.aura.build/learn/introduction"},{label:"Lovable credits",href:"https://docs.lovable.dev/introduction/plans-and-credits"},{label:"Lovable design templates",href:"https://docs.lovable.dev/features/business/design-templates"},{label:"Figma Make docs",href:"https://help.figma.com/hc/en-us/articles/31304412302231-Explore-Figma-Make"},{label:"v0 pricing",href:"https://v0.app/pricing"}],KGs="Compare Aura, Lovable, Figma Make, and v0 for AI website generation, pro 